      "actual_eos_at_stop": true,
      "answer_segment": "To determine how much Tom's restaurant makes in a week, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the daily revenue from one reservation.\n2. Calculate the weekly revenue from one reservation.\n3. Calculate the weekly revenue from all reservations.\n4. Calculate the weekly revenue from the wine sales.\n5. Add the daily revenue from the meals and the weekly revenue from the wine sales to get the total weekly revenue.\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n1. The cost of the meals for one reservation is:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 5 = 10 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n2. The cost of the wine for one reservation is:\n   \\[\n   5 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n3. Therefore, the total revenue from one reservation is:\n   \\[\n   10 + 5 = 15 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n4. Since the restaurant is open 2 days a week, the weekly revenue from one reservation is:\n   \\[\n   15 \\times 2 = 30 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n5. The total revenue from all reservations in a week is:\n   \\[\n   30 \\times 7 = 210 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n6. The total revenue from the wine sales in a week is:\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 7 = 35 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n7. Therefore, the total weekly revenue from both the meals and the wine is:\n   \\[\n   210 + 35 = 245 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the total amount Tom's restaurant makes in a week is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{245}\n\\]",
