      "actual_eos_at_stop": true,
      "answer_segment": "To determine the age of John's youngest son in 3 years, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine James's current age:**\n   - James is currently twice as old as his sister Dora.\n   - Dora will turn 12 in 3 years, so her current age is \\(12 - 3 = 9\\) years.\n   - Therefore, James's current age is \\(2 \\times 9 = 18\\) years.\n\n2. **Determine John's current age:**\n   - John was 19 years old when he had James.\n   - The difference in age between John and James is \\(19 - 9 = 10\\) years.\n   - Since James is currently 18 years old, John's current age is \\(18 + 10 = 28\\) years.\n\n3. **Determine the age of John's youngest son in 3 years:**\n   - John's youngest son was born when John was 32 years old.\n   - The age difference between John and his youngest son is \\(32 - 9 = 23\\) years.\n   - Therefore, in 3 years, John's youngest son will be \\(9 + 3 = 12\\) years old.\n\nThus, the age of John's youngest son in 3 years will be \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
