      "actual_eos_at_stop": true,
      "answer_segment": "To determine how many more oranges Ana will have peeled than Jane after an hour, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total time available:**\n   An hour is 60 minutes.\n\n2. **Determine the rate at which each person peels oranges:**\n   - Ana peels an orange in 3 minutes.\n   - Jane peels an orange in 4 minutes.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of oranges each person can peel in an hour:**\n   - For Ana:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Number of oranges Ana can peel} = \\frac{60 \\text{ minutes}}{3 \\text{ minutes/orange}} = 20 \\text{ oranges}\n     \\]\n   - For Jane:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Number of oranges Jane can peel} = \\frac{60 \\text{ minutes}}{4 \\text{ minutes/orange}} = 15 \\text{ oranges}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Find the difference in the number of oranges peeled by Ana and Jane:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Difference} = 20 \\text{ oranges} - 15 \\text{ oranges} = 5 \\text{ oranges}\n   \\]\n\nThus, after an hour, Ana will have peeled \\(\\boxed{5}\\) more oranges than Jane.",
